From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: contracts: use the zod 3 API through zod/v3

Built with npm instead of pnpm, contracts' zod ^3.24 is resolved against
the hoisted zod 4.6.5 that packages/shared pins, and code written against
the zod 3 API fails to compile. zod 3.25.28+ and every zod 4 release provide
that API as "zod/v3", which zod-to-json-schema 3.25 already imports; using
it the same way lets contracts build against either major. The 564 tool
JSON schemas sent to providers are byte-identical before and after.

Patch-mainline: No

